counterfactuals.output:
1. A clutch power transmission device comprising:

a housing defining an interior chamber;

a power transmission hub disposed at least partially within the interior chamber and rotatable relative to the housing;

a clutch pack positioned within the interior chamber and operatively arranged between the housing and the power transmission hub, the clutch pack including a plurality of alternating friction disks coupled respectively to the housing and to the power transmission hub; and

a piston module disposed within the housing and configured to selectively apply an axial force to the clutch pack to engage the alternating friction disks for transmitting torque between the housing and the power transmission hub,

wherein the piston module includes two or more pistons arranged to act on the clutch pack, the two or more pistons being selectively actuable to vary an engagement force applied to the clutch pack.

A power transmission device comprising:

a clutch housing configured to receive torque from a drive source;

a clutch hub disposed radially inward of the clutch housing and configured to transmit torque to an output member;

a disk housing disposed with respect to the clutch housing and the clutch hub;

a plurality of friction engagement elements including first friction plates supported by one of the clutch housing and the clutch hub and second friction plates supported by the other of the clutch housing and the clutch hub, the first and second friction plates being alternately arranged in an axial direction;

a plurality of hydraulic pistons disposed to apply an axial pressing force to the friction engagement elements in response to supplied hydraulic pressure, thereby selectively engaging the friction engagement elements to transmit torque between the clutch housing and the clutch hub; and

a plurality of springs configured to bias at least one of the hydraulic pistons and the friction engagement elements in a disengaging direction, the springs including return springs for returning the hydraulic pistons when hydraulic pressure is released and/or separating springs for separating adjacent friction plates to reduce drag during disengagement.
